{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Oil</b> — for anointing, and fragrance — to smell — gives joy to the heart. And so the sweetness of one's fellow gives joy to the heart, by way of the counsel that his soul counsels him: the sweetness of a secret, as one who counsels his own soul — the sweetness gladdens him. As in: who together sweeten a secret; consult the sweetness of a secret."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The final phrase 'נתייעץ מתק סוד' is cryptic and possibly corrupt; rendered hyper-literally. The reference 'אשר יחדיו נמתיק סוד' appears to cite Psalm 55:15."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:02.756594069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}